- 2a: arow[l] = sM[(br+i)*kCs + br + l]: lane j varies → different i per lane (i from j) — each lane reads its own row — (br+i)*64 + br + l — lanes have different i and different l (l from j..i-1 — loop bounds differ per lane!) — divergent loops + scattered LDS — conflicts possible but small phase.
- Gram phase writes sN[t*kCs + j], sM[t*kCs + j]: threads own different (t,j) — scattered 4B writes → conflicts possible; small.

So the dominant fix is sC padding: Rb*(D+1)?? Hmm — but wait, D=16/32 (template) also: D=16: stride 17 ✓; D=32: stride 33 ✓; D=64: 65; D=128: 129. Padding by +1 float per row fixes the bank conflicts in the u/o inner loops.

